      {
        "text": "# .then()\n\n`.then()` is a method that runs a block of code only after the Promise is **fulfilled**. It receives the data from the Promise so you can use it.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/09a831dba196e13a406cbf66abfe213f-Vocab Images.png",
        "key": "designing-reliable-apps-lesson3-level3-test_2025-pilot-a7d47b7b-ef03-4566-8998-518e074e2c10",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "text": "# .catch()\n\n`.catch()` is a method that runs a block of code only if the Promise is **rejected**. It receives the error message explaining what went wrong so your app doesn't crash.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/ed562a49342bb59a8bdd929b6abf77a0-then Images.png",
